CLAIM: CUB K=29 final seeds 1–3: lateroll averages 81.39% versus MaskedKD’s 80.22%, paired difference +1.17 pp [0.75, 1.58], below the 1.92 pp promotion threshold; both report approximately 12.99 GFLOPs/img.
VERDICT: NEEDS-MORE
REASON: The six cited metrics support the accuracy comparison, including final_lateroll_k29_s1_1101_104303_ef38 versus final_maskedkd_k29_s1_1101_104303_b676; costs match only after rounding (12.9900 versus 12.9881). Historical lock verification for 3b594cc1646f and 8ac8a710a4ae is missing; the researcher’s explanation and commit subjects do not independently establish equivalence to the current lock.
Missing also are the pre-method PROPOSALS/selector-addition history and underlying mandatory baseline metrics; narrowing the claim does not waive those checks. The table flags ToMe as unmatched, and the parent advantage (+0.94 pp) remains below threshold. Decomposition supports teacher-fidelity effects, not causal attribution of trained accuracy gains. Novelty is weak: the source implements a truncated version of established [attention rollout](https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.385.pdf).